We'll use a relational database to track user progress and provide historical data for the frontend.
Core Tables
users_loyalty
Tracks the current state of a user.

| Column | Type | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| wallet_address | VARCHAR(44) | Primary Key (Solana Address). |
| current_balance | BIGINT | Points available to spend. |
| lifetime_points | BIGINT | Total earned (used for Tier calculation). |
| tier_id | INT | Foreign Key to loyalty_tiers. |

points_ledger
An immutable audit log of every point movement.

| Column | Type | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| id | UUID | Unique transaction ID. |
| wallet_address | VARCHAR(44) | Recipient. |
| amount | BIGINT | Positive for earned, negative for spent. |
| tx_signature | TEXT | The Solana transaction hash (link to on-chain). |
| reason | VARCHAR | e.g., "purchase", "referral", "reward_redemption". |

⚡ 4. The Indexing Logic (The "Watcher")
We need a background worker that listens to the Solana blockchain. If a user receives points directly on-chain (or if our API succeeds), the database must stay in sync.